# Sample for the tests (locally and in CI): a plain `go test ./...` checks
# only these puzzles, `STARBATTLE_ALL_HARD=1 go test ./...` all of
# bibliothek.idx.
# It covers sizes 5 to 15, every rule (Pigeonhole and DeadCells too, with and
# without lookahead) and every rating, up to the deepest thought experiment of
# the library (n13_s4661). Solving it takes about a twelfth of the whole library
# (21 of 254 s, one puzzle at a time); left out are the most expensive ones
# (n14_s1262, n15_s1068, n13_s1787, 8 to 13 s each).
# The cheap ones come first: with -short some tests take only the first few.
#
# 1 star, solved by all rules without lookahead:
n05_s029.txt  # smallest, library no. 1
n08_s087.txt  # many Confinement steps
n11_s059.txt  # many ForcedPartner steps
n12_s005.txt  # DeadCells even without lookahead
n06_s071.txt
n07_s005.txt
n09_s017.txt
n10_s047.txt
#
# 2 stars, need lookahead even with all rules:
n10_s396.txt   # smallest with lookahead (9 steps)
n12_s082.txt   # many DeadCells steps, short
n13_s181.txt   # N = 13
n14_s024.txt   # N = 14, the cheapest of that size
n10_s1330.txt  # chain of 5
n11_s3184.txt  # 9 steps
n12_s1954.txt
n13_s4124.txt  # chain of 6
n13_s783.txt   # 9 steps
n14_s1525.txt  # 9 steps, chain of 6
n15_s485.txt   # N = 15, the cheapest of that size
#
# 3 stars:
n11_s095.txt   # Pigeonhole, 11 lookahead steps
n10_s1271.txt  # 18 steps, chain of 6
n11_s504.txt   # chain of 7
n12_s1503.txt  # 17 steps
n13_s3567.txt  # chain of 6
n14_s1717.txt  # chain of 7
n14_s155.txt   # 25 steps
n14_s2876.txt  # 25 steps, chain of 8
n15_s130.txt   # N = 15, 14 steps
n13_s4661.txt  # 41 steps, chain of 9 (the deepest), 6 s
